{"name":"Rain Drum","hex":"#685346","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Condensed water falling from a cloud.","Any matter moving or falling, usually through air, and especially if liquid or otherwise figuratively identifiable with raindrops."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have rain fall from the sky.","To fall as or like rain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rain"},{"term":"drum","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A percussive musical instrument spanned with a thin covering on at least one end for striking, forming an acoustic chamber; a membranophone.","Any similar hollow, cylindrical object."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To beat a drum.","To beat with a rapid succession of strokes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bronze drum","blocks":[{"text":"Bronze drums are ancient artifacts found in various cultures in Southeast Asia and southern China. The drums were cast in bronze using the lost-wax casting method. The drums were both musical instruments and cult objects. They are decorated with geometric patterns, scenes of daily life and war, animals and birds, and boats. Bronze drums are considered one of the national symbols of Vietnam."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Ngoc_Lu_bronze_drum_surface.gif/330px-Ngoc_Lu_bronze_drum_surface.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bronze_drum","wikidata":"Q10829913"},{"title":"Rain","blocks":[{"text":"Rain or rainfall is a form of atmospheric precipitation composed of droplets of water aerosols that have condensed from atmospheric water vapor and fall by gravity. Depending on the intensity, rain can be described as a drizzle, a shower, a cloudburst or a downpour. It is also often accompanied by other weather phenomena such as strong wind (rainstorm) and lightning (thunderstorm), and may be mixed with hail/ice pellet, snow (sleet) and sandstorm. Rain is a major component of the water cycle and is responsible for depositing most of the fresh water on Earth. It provides water for hydroelectric power plants, crop irrigation, and suitable conditions for many types of ecosystems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg/330px-Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rain","wikidata":"Q7925"},{"title":"Drum","blocks":[{"text":"The drum is a member of the percussion group of musical instruments. In the Hornbostel–Sachs classification system, it is a membranophone. Drums consist of at least one membrane, called a drumhead or drum skin, that is stretched over a shell and struck, either directly with the player's hands, or with a percussion mallet, to produce sound. There is usually a resonant head on the underside of the drum. Other techniques have been used to cause drums to make sound, such as the thumb roll. Drums are the world's oldest and most ubiquitous musical instruments, and the basic design has remained virtually unchanged for thousands of years."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/DrumMozartRegiment.jpg/330px-DrumMozartRegiment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drum","wikidata":"Q11404"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Trong_dong_Dong_Son.jpg/500px-Trong_dong_Dong_Son.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Trong_dong_Dong_Son.jpg/1280px-Trong_dong_Dong_Son.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Trong_dong_Dong_Son.jpg/500px-Trong_dong_Dong_Son.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Đông Sơn drum in Guimet Museum, Paris","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATrong_dong_Dong_Son.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Dong_Son_drums.jpg/250px-Dong_Son_drums.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/eb/Dong_Son_drums.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Dong_Son_drums.jpg/250px-Dong_Son_drums.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Castings on the Ngọc Lũ drum's surface","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADong_Son_drums.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Western_Han_Bronze_Cowrie_Container_1.jpg/500px-Western_Han_Bronze_Cowrie_Container_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Western_Han_Bronze_Cowrie_Container_1.jpg/1280px-Western_Han_Bronze_Cowrie_Container_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Western_Han_Bronze_Cowrie_Container_1.jpg/500px-Western_Han_Bronze_Cowrie_Container_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Dian bronze drum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWestern_Han_Bronze_Cowrie_Container_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Bronze_drum_with_frogs.jpg/500px-Bronze_drum_with_frogs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Bronze_drum_with_frogs.jpg/1280px-Bronze_drum_with_frogs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_c